# Workflow: ptrm

This workflow `ptrm` open port in remote server to connect LLM service

## Context

- OS/Kernel: Windows 

## Workflow

```makefile

ptrm_table:
    # Description: read/view ptrm table to select entry which match user intent by <NOTES>
    # Command: `cat ~/echo-home/.vim/pages/$(hostname).ptrm.md | head -n -2`
    # Output: <SSH_HOST>, <LOCAL_PORT>, <REMOTE_IP>, <REMOTE_PORT> , <NOTES>
ptrm_exec: ptrm_table
    # Description: open port
    # Command: `wingterm "port-remote <SSH_HOST> <LOCAL_PORT> <REMOTE_IP> <REMOTE_PORT>"`
    # Success: no error in output
    # Failure: any error
    # Input: <REMOTE_IP> , default `127.0.0.1`
ptrm_verify: ptrm_exec
    # Description: Test if port is reachable
    # Command: `curl -v http://127.0.0.1:<LOCAL_PORT>`
    # Success: "Established" or "Connected" in output
    # Failure: error
```
